<p>This page describes how BlessBoard handles information on <strong>blessboard.com</strong> and how that relates to individual church sites on the platform. It is an informational overview — not a substitute for counsel from your church or legal advisors.</p>
<%# Legal approval still required before replacing this overview with formal policy text — see docs/blessboard-legal-review-gaps.md %>

<h2>BlessBoard.com (platform website)</h2>
<p>When you browse blessboard.com, BlessBoard may process:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Church finder preference.</strong> If you select a church, a cookie named <code>bb_church_pref</code> may store the public church and branch slugs you chose so you can return to the same selection. It does not sign you in.</li>
  <li><strong>Directory search.</strong> Search terms you enter on <a href="/churches">Find a Church</a> are used to show matching active congregations. They are not stored as a separate marketing analytics log in the directory feature.</li>
  <li><strong>Contact and onboarding forms.</strong> If you submit <a href="/contact">Contact BlessBoard</a> or <a href="/register-church">Register Your Church</a>, BlessBoard stores the details you provide (such as name, email, phone, church information, and message) together with basic submission metadata needed to review the request.</li>
</ul>
<p>BlessBoard.com public pages do not load third-party analytics trackers. The site may load fonts from Google Fonts to display typography.</p>

<h2>Authenticated sessions</h2>
<p>When you sign in to a BlessBoard administrator console or a church member, leader, or admin portal, the application uses a session cookie (<code>getpro_sid</code>) backed by the platform database. Session cookies are intended to keep you signed in during your visit and are not used for advertising.</p>

<h2>Church tenant sites</h2>
<p>Each congregation on BlessBoard operates on its own church site (typically a dedicated hostname per branch). On those sites, your church may collect member registration details, public contact form messages, and authenticated portal activity according to that congregation’s own practices.</p>
<p>For questions about how <em>your church</em> uses member or visitor information, contact your church administrators directly using the Contact page on your congregation’s site.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<ul>
  <li>You can clear a remembered church selection from the BlessBoard homepage or by visiting <a href="/churches">Find a Church</a> and choosing another congregation.</li>
  <li>You can reach BlessBoard platform administrators through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.</li>
</ul>

